# The ledger of `chart`: plots and charts made as SVG text and as images,
# one block per capability, and what Heroes answers to each.
#
# Go 1.27, Rust 1.100 and Python 3.15 carry no chart in their standard
# libraries. Their charting libraries are not on this Mac (no gonum/plot in
# the Go module cache, no plotters in Cargo's registry), and fetching one is a
# download this round has no leave for, so the `go` and `rust` columns are
# `-` and say nothing of those libraries. The yardstick is Python's
# matplotlib 3.10.9, installed on this Mac outside the tree and read there on
# 2026-11-24: the 164 functions `matplotlib.pyplot` defines itself, listed
# by `dir()` and `inspect`, each in a block or in the dropped section; its
# classes and the modules it re-exports are its object layer, dropped below.
#
# The oracles the tests were held to, run the same day: d3-array 3.2.4,
# d3-scale 4.0.2 and d3-time 3.1.0 under Node 26 (their `ticks`, linear
# `nice` and `tickFormat`, `log.ticks` and `log.tickFormat`, `scaleUtc`'s
# ticks, format and `nice`, and `bin`) over 71 cases, every value, label and
# range equal but the one widening `bin` names; NumPy 2.5.4's `histogram`
# over 154 bins, all equal; and each chart's SVG rendered by CairoSVG 2.9.1
# and resvg 0.5.0 against the image the package drew of the same layout,
# with text as outlines within a mean of 0.3 levels and no pixel off by more
# than a quarter.
#
# The test font, `chart/internal/samples.hero`, is Noto Sans Regular 2.015,
# Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License
# 1.1, whose text the font's own `name` table holds.

## Series over two axes

capability chart/line  a line through a series' points in their order, broken where a value is not a number
  heroes  chart.Mark.line, chart.lay_out
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  plot
  note    a value that is not a number breaks the line, as matplotlib masks it; an infinite one is `invalid`

capability chart/scatter  a disc at each point of a series
  heroes  chart.Mark.points
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  scatter
  note    one size and one colour a series; a disc whose centre falls outside the plot is not drawn, one inside is drawn whole

capability chart/line-and-points  a line through a series' points with a disc at each
  heroes  chart.Mark.line_and_points
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  plot
  note    matplotlib's marker styles beyond the disc are left out

capability chart/area  the room between a series' line and zero filled, see-through where areas overlap
  heroes  chart.Mark.area
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  fill_between, fill
  note    filled at two fifths of the series' colour, a gap parting the area

capability chart/stacked-area  areas stacked, each on the ones before it
  heroes  chart.Plot.stacked
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  stackplot
  note    stacked areas share their columns and hold numbers, or `invalid`; stacked as matplotlib's and d3's default stacks them, values added in order

## Bars and histograms

capability chart/bars  bars of categories side by side, a series each
  heroes  chart.Bars, chart.Grouping.grouped
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  bar
  note    a value that is not a number makes no bar; the value axis spans zero unless its range is fixed

capability chart/stacked-bars  bars of several series stacked in each category
  heroes  chart.Grouping.stacked
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  bar, barh
  note    the positive values stack up from zero and the negative down, as d3's diverging offset stacks them, so no two bars overlap; matplotlib stacks what its `bottom` says

capability chart/horizontal-bars  bars lying along the value axis, the categories down the left side
  heroes  chart.Direction.horizontal
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  barh
  note    the first category at the top, as a list reads; matplotlib puts it at the bottom

capability chart/bins  values counted into a histogram's bins
  heroes  chart.bin
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  hist
  note    `auto` is d3's default (Sturges' count at nice edges), `count` NumPy's equal widths and `edges` NumPy's own edges; values all one widen to one bin from half below to half above, as NumPy widens them, where d3 makes a bin of no width

capability chart/histogram  a histogram drawn: its bins as bars on a value axis
  heroes  chart.Histogram
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  hist
  note    the bars touch, a pixel's gap between them; one colour

## Pies

capability chart/pie  a pie: slices clockwise from twelve o'clock, each its value's share
  heroes  chart.Pie
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  pie
  note    clockwise from twelve as d3-shape's pie turns, where matplotlib starts at three and turns the other way; a slice's share is written on it where the text fits inside the slice

capability chart/donut  a donut: a pie with a hole a share of its radius
  heroes  chart.Pie.hole
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  pie

## Axes and ticks

capability chart/linear-ticks  a linear axis's ticks at steps of 1, 2 or 5 times a power of ten, labelled
  heroes  chart.ticks
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  xticks, yticks, locator_params, tick_params, ticklabel_format
  note    d3's ticks and `,f` labels, equal over the oracle's cases; the minus sign is the ASCII hyphen where d3 writes U+2212

capability chart/nice-range  an axis's range moved out to its ticks
  heroes  chart.nice
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  autoscale, margins, axis
  note    d3's `nice`, where matplotlib pads the data by a margin instead

capability chart/log-scale  a logarithmic axis in any base above 1, its powers and their multiples ticked
  heroes  chart.Scale.log
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  xscale, yscale, loglog, semilogx, semilogy, minorticks_on, minorticks_off
  note    d3's `log.ticks` and its choice of labelled ticks; a base whose multiples would pass ten times the count asked takes linear ticks; a value at or below zero is `invalid`, where matplotlib masks it

capability chart/time-scale  a time axis in UTC ticked at the calendar's steps and labelled by them
  heroes  chart.Scale.time
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  plot_date
  note    d3's `scaleUtc` ticks and multi-scale labels in English, years 1 to 9999; a time zone's local calendar is left out

capability chart/fixed-range  an axis's range given, what falls outside cut away
  heroes  chart.Extent.fixed
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  xlim, ylim

capability chart/grid  lines of a grid at an axis's labelled ticks
  heroes  chart.Axis.grid
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  grid

capability chart/legend  the named series listed beside the plot, each with its mark
  heroes  chart.Look.legend
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  legend, figlegend
  note    beside the plot, in as many columns as its height needs, never over the data

capability chart/title-and-labels  a title over the plot and a label on each axis
  heroes  chart.Look.title, chart.Axis.label
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  title, suptitle, xlabel, ylabel

capability chart/layout  margins measured from the text in the font, crowded tick labels thinned
  heroes  chart.lay_out
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tight_layout, subplots_adjust

capability chart/palette  colours for the series, of hues evenly spaced and each far from the one before
  heroes  chart.palette
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    made in `image/colorspace`'s HLS; matplotlib's colour cycle is a fixed list in its settings

## Written out

capability chart/svg  a chart written as an SVG document, its text as text or as outlines
  heroes  chart.to_svg
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  savefig
  note    one line, no XML declaration; text elements name the font's family, outlines draw alike in every reader

capability chart/image  a chart drawn into an RGBA image, anti-aliased, its text in the font
  heroes  chart.to_image
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  savefig
  note    the same drawing as the SVG; writing it as PNG is `image/png`'s

